      "basis": "VERIFIED DIRECTLY, TIER A, with the edition named. The table's own title states that Russia's revenue and KOSGU classification codes are mapped onto the classification «установленным Руководством по статистике государственных финансов (СГФ - 2014)» (\"established by the Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM 2014)\"). «СГФ - 2014» is GFSM 2014, matching the `imf-gfsm` node exactly. `methodology_depends_on`: the Russian classification codes are made to conform to the GFSM 2014 revenue classification for reporting purposes, which is method rather than citation. TWO WEAKNESSES STATED PLAINLY, and the reason this is minted from the table rather than from Приказ 128н: (a) the citation is in the TITLE of a methodological correspondence table, not in the operative text of a numbered order -- the operative text of 128н and its Порядок were searched and name only unversioned, plural «руководствами», which is why no GFSM edge is drawn from that node; (b) the workbook is republished annually at a year-stamped URL that will move, though the «(СГФ - 2014)» wording has been stable across the 2024, 2025 and 2026 editions.",
